## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP over subsequences with a fixed length and pairwise costs, plus explicit reconstruction. It moves beyond contiguous partitions by requiring last-step linkage through prior picks.

## Key Concepts
- Subsequence DP with fixed length
- Min-over-predecessor recurrence
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and practical optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function solve(A, m){
  const n=A.length;
  const dp=Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(m+1).fill(Infinity));
  const par=Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(m+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[i][1]=0;
  for(let t=2;t<=m;t++){
    for(let i=t-1;i<n;i++){
      for(let j=t-2;j<i;j++){
        const c=dp[j][t-1]+Math.abs(A[i]-A[j]);
        if(c<dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=c; par[i][t]=j; }
      }
    }
  }
  let best=Infinity,bestI=-1;
  for(let i=m-1;i<n;i++){ if(dp[i][m]<best){ best=dp[i][m]; bestI=i; } }
  const path=[];
  let cur=bestI, t=m;
  while(t>=1){
    path.push(cur);
    cur=par[cur][t];
    t--;
  }
  path.reverse();
  return {cost:best, indices:path};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
The task tests a non-trivial DP where block value is a segment maximum, not sum. It requires precomputing segment maxima and careful reconstruction, exposing trade-offs between time and memory.

## Key Concepts
- DP on prefixes with exact block counts
- Transition uses max(A[j..i])
- Precompute M[j][i] in O(n^2)
- Reconstruction pointers for endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSumKBlocks(A, k){
  const n=A.length;
  const M=Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(n).fill(0));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){ let m=-Infinity; for(let j=i;j>=0;j--){ m=Math.max(m,A[j]); M[j][i]=m; } }
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const split=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(k,i);t++){
      for(let j=1;j<=i;j++){
        const val=dp[j-1][t-1]+M[j-1][i-1];
        if(val>dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; split[i][t]=j; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {best:dp[n][k]};
}
```

